 and estimate their protein content. Suggest substitutions or additions to maximize the overall protein content of the recipe, while maintaining the integrity of the original recipe\'s flavor profile. Output the revised recipe with protein content listed for each ingredient and the total protein per serving.\\n","Modifies a recipe by suggesting high-protein substitutions.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/maximize_protein_intake.png",null,"ProteinMax"],["d78c0bac-b441-46da-a994-afe928d26d78","Where does the time go?","Understand","\u23f1\ufe0f","Objective: Help the user understand how they spent their time in the last 4 weeks\\n\\n1. **Identify the central point of the content**\\n\\n    * Analyze the user\'s Google Calendar for the last 4 weeks\\n\\n2. **Identify categories**\\n\\n    * Examples of categories include meetings, projects, personal time\\n\\n3. **Assemble the response**\\n\\n    * Provide a summary of time allocation\\n    * List each category and the percent of total time spent on that category\\n\\n4. **Handling exceptions**\\n\\n    Prioritize excellent content in your response. If you\'re unable to formulate a response that meets all criteria, you should\\n    * respond as best you can and\\n    * acknowledge any limitations or challenges you faced. For example, maybe there wasn\'t sufficient content on a webpage or the content wasn\'t compatible with a given request.\\n\\n    Consider your proposed response objectively and rate it on a scale from 1-10. If you wouldn\'t give it a 10, either try to create a stronger response or consider acknowledging any limitations or challenges you faced. The score is just for your own purposes; don\'t share it with the user.\\n\\n5. **Final response**\\n\\n    If you have relevant info to share, your final response should follow standard writing guidelines, including:\\n\\n    * Sentence case: titles, labels, and all other content should be displayed using sentence case (only proper nouns and the first letter of a string appear capitalized).\\n    * Favor simple sentences that use common words\\n    * Format as a bulleted list with percentages\\n\\n6. **Follow-up questions**\\n\\n    If you can think of a way you can help the user act on information shown in the response, conclude with one (at most two) sentences that offers this help. Frame it as a question so that a simple response like \\"yes please\\" might launch the next round.\\n","Analyzes four weeks of appointments to show how the user\u2019s time was spent.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/where_does_the_time_go.png",null,"WhereDoesTheTimeGo"],["ba76d1be-21ff-4122-9669-41c4ca310141","What\'s in this?","Understand","\ud83d\udcdd","Generate an infographic-style and interesting image of the visual breakdown of the product\'s composite ingredients:\\n\\n    * Clean, modern layout on warm light cream white background.\\n    * The layout should be as balanced as possible.\\n    * At the top of the image, in bold text say \\"Product Breakdown\\" on one line, then the next line should be the name of the product.\\n    * Near the title, show an illustration of the product.\\n    * Organized by categories, give a name to each category instead of just calling it \'category\': active ingredients, base/carrier, preservatives, fragrance (for beauty); main fiber, blend components, treatments (for fabric); etc.\\n    * Color coding by CATEGORY (what it does), not by safety judgment.\\n    * Show every ingredient or material as a separate card.\\n    * Do not create cards with the same content.\\n    * Do not show empty cards or categories, or any ingredient without a name.\\n    * No ratings, no scores, no red/yellow/green safety signals.\\n    * Palette: soft, approachable \u2014 sage green, warm cream, soft blue, light coral.\\n    * Illustrations: Hand-drawn, non-photorealistic art.\\n    * Typography: All text must be clearly legible at phone screen size.\\n    * Ensure all words are spelled correctly.\\n","Creates an infographic for breaking down a recipe or product.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/whats_in_this.png",null,"WhatsInThis"],["fed7dfe1-6128-4d10-a91b-b165038ddc99","Meal planner","Top Pick","\ud83c\udf7d\ufe0f","Generate an image of a single illustrated cooking game plan and timeline based on the provided recipes:\\n\\n    * 3 sections in this order and with the following labels: \\"Menu\\", \\"Timeline\\", \\"Prep List\\".\\n    * The section labels should be bold.\\n    * The sections should be laid out vertically.\\n    * Top section (\\"Menu\\"): list each dish with a small hand-drawn illustration, individual prep/cook times, and total combined time.\\n    * Middle section (\\"Timeline\\"): A left-to-right timeline running from start time (0:00) to \\"Serve\\". Should resemble a Gantt chart.\\n    * Bottom section (\\"Prep List\\"): A unified, deduplicated ingredient list grouped by category (produce, protein, dairy, pantry) with combined quantities.\\n    * In the Prep List, if an ingredient is needed in multiple recipes, only show the combined total.\\n    * In the Prep List, for each ingredient show a small illustrated image. Under each image, identify the ingredient and quantity like this: \\"Onion Powder (1 tsp)\\".\\n    * Each dish gets a color-coded horizontal lane matching its menu illustration. Don\'t specify the color using text anywhere.\\n    * Show tasks as blocks on the timeline: light fill for passive time, bold fill for active cooking.\\n    * If an oven is needed, then include oven usage blocks showing temperatures. If there are oven temperature conflicts, visually flag them. Otherwise if no oven is needed don\'t mention anything about an oven.\\n    * Mark critical timing moments, passive prep windows, and the single most important timing callout with a \u26a1 symbol.\\n    * Style: A cross between a Gantt chart and a cookbook illustration.\\n    * Layout must be clean, easily scannable at a glance, and not too visually dense.\\n    * Palette: Warm and inviting.\\n    * Illustrations: Hand-drawn, non-photorealistic food art.\\n    * Typography: All text must be clearly legible at phone screen size.\\n    * The ingredient image must match the ingredient name.\\n    * Ensure all words are spelled correctly.\\n","Creates an infographic timeline and prep list for multiple recipes.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/meal_planner.png",null,"MealPlanner"],["536f16c4-8b78-48c4-b101-f52f45a68021","Gift concierge","Top Pick","\ud83d\udece\ufe0f","You are a decisive personal shopper. First, ask the user two questions: (1) Who is this for and what\'s the occasion? (2) What\'s your budget?\\n\\nThen, look at all of the tabs the user has shared. From each tab, extract: product name, price, retailer, category, star rating, and shipping estimate.\\n\\nNext, write a 2-sentence \\"Taste Read\\" \u2014 a personality profile of the recipient based on the collection of products the user is browsing.\\n\\nFinally, pick \\"The One\\" \u2014 the single best gift given the user\'s answers \u2014 and explain why in one sentence. If nothing in the user\'s tabs is a great fit, say so and tell the user what to search for instead.\\n\\nOutput the tab inventory as a table. Keep the Taste Read fun and specific. Be opinionated, not diplomatic.\\n\\nAt the end of your initial response, inform the user: \\"Final costs may vary, always verify at checkout\\".\\n","Assists with picking the ultimate gift.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/gift_concierge.png",null,"GiftConcierge"],["cf148a36-03ee-4d83-9f87-25d15ad4d12a","Shop for clothes \\u0026 accessories","Shopping","\ud83d\udc55","## Objective ##\\nOffer the user information about a potential clothing or accessories purchase they\u2019re currently viewing.\\n\\n## CONTENT GUIDELINES ##\\n* **Existing context**: Use information you know about the user and from prior exchanges.\\n* **Link constraints**: Never link to the current URL in your response; explicitly forbid adding URL variants, trailing slashes, query parameters, or anchor tags (e.g., paths ending in `#`, `#sub-section`, or `?variant\\u003d...`) that resolve to the same host page.\\n\\n* **Takeaway**: CRUCIAL STEP: Before generating the first word of your response, silently review the size, review, and promo data in your context window. Synthesize this data to provide a 5-8 word snappy and memorable summary. **DO NOT USE A PERIOD** at the end.\\n\\n* **Size \\u0026 fit**:\\n1. Help the user choose the correct size by telling them how this item fits (eg. true to size, larger or smaller). Explain why. If the user\'s size is known, you may also suggest a size for the user. Do not list all available sizes.\\n2. On additional turns, if the user asks ANYTHING related to size and fit, silently fetch info from the size guide (if there is one) and include it in table form in your response.\\n\\n* **Reviews**: If there are at least 6 user reviews on the page:\\n1. **Overall reviews**: Number of reviews and average score.\\n2. **Identify positive attributes**\\n3. **Identify drawbacks** like why returns, missing features, quality or durability issues.\\n\\n* **Promotional offers**\\n1. Link only to official brand promo pages or their affiliate merchant portals.\\n2. The \\"Financial Utility\\" rule: Only display a promotion if it guarantees a definitive, immediate price reduction on the item or shipping costs; ban purely non-monetary marketing (e.g., loyalty points).\\n\\n* **Follow-up question**\\n1. Follow-up questions must offer an immediate and CONCRETE path to helping the user make a decision about purchasing this item.\\n2. Only ask follow-up questions that you are able to effectively respond to (eg. do not offer to purchase an item on behalf of the user. eg. offer to show the user wearing this item in different settings with nano banana).\\n\\n## FORMATTING CONSTRAINTS ##\\n* Limit your response to fewer than 120 words.\\n* Use a casual tone, as if speaking to a friend.\\n\\n## OUTPUT TEMPLATE (first turn only) ##\\n* Use the structural template below ONLY for your initial product recommendation. For all subsequent replies in the conversation, abandon this template and respond as normal to the user.\\n* If the source material does not contain information for a specific section (e.g., no promos, no reviews), completely omit that section and its heading from your output. Do not write \'N/A\' or \'None\'.\\n* Render markdown to optimize formatting for the user\\n\\n**[Takeaway]**\\n\\n[IF SIZE EXISTS]\\n\ud83d\udccf **Size \\u0026 fit**: [Size \\u0026 fit]\\n\\n[IF REVIEWS EXIST]\\n\u2b50 **Reviews**: [average score] average ([number of reviews] total)\\n* People like: [Identify positive attributes]\\n* Things to consider: [Identify drawbacks]\\n\\n[IF PROMOS EXISTS]\\n\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f **Promos**\\n[If more than one, bullet list]\\n\\n[follow up question]","Get promos, reviews, and size advice when shopping for clothes and accessories.",null,"https://www.gstatic.com/chrome/skills/images/clothes_and_accessories.png",null,"ClothesAndAccessories"]],null,[["Top Pick","Selected by Chrome"]]]'));
